Recommends: keyd
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: Per-game key remapping for the Razer Tartarus V2 keypad
 tartarus remaps the keys of a Razer Tartarus V2 gaming keypad on a
 per-game basis. Profiles name the keypad's physical keys rather than HID
 scancodes, and are compiled into a keyd configuration and applied without
 rebuilding the udev hardware database.
 .
 It includes a terminal editor that draws the keypad, so bindings can be
 changed by moving over the key and pressing the one it should send.
 .
 Profiles for several games are installed under
 /usr/share/tartarus/profiles and are used as read-only defaults; copies in
 ~/.config/tartarus/profiles take precedence.
 .
 Applying a profile requires keyd, which is recommended rather than
 depended upon so the package remains installable where keyd is not
 available.
